{
  "dom_id": "step-q49123",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "$\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x(6\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C, \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x(6\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{csc}^{2}⁡x-5\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 6{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 5\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)-5(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+5\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
